      "object": "This study highlights the complex interplay of psychological, socioeconomic, and sport-related factors contributing to the risk of eating disorders (ED) and disordered eating (DE) among Taekwondo athletes. Mental health challenges such as depression, anxiety, and ADHD emerged as significant predictors of disordered eating behaviors. Additionally, unemployment and fluctuations in income were found to influence the risk of ED and DE, reflecting the broader impact of economic stress on athlete well-being."
